                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Vikings risen from the dead - want to beat, cut into thin slices and enjoy the violence in the Arena!\n\n[list][b]Pros:[/b]\n[*]+ Availability: the game is free\n[*]+ Multiple battle arenas\n[*]+ Many opponents\n[*]+ Unique visual style\n[*]+ Localization into many languages\n[*]+ Gamepad support\n[*]+ Simultaneous play for up to 4 players!\n[*]+ Remote Play Together\n[*]+ Demo level of the original game\n[*]+ Multiple arena modes\n\n[b]Minuses:[/b]\n[*]- Demo game\n[*]- Bug with sound: the volume may decrease during the game, and then return\n[*]- FPS drops\n[*]- 4 heroes instead of 8\n[*]- Bug in which subtitles close the game menu\n[*]- White subtitles on white background[/list]\n\n[b]Total:[/b]\nIt's kind of funny that this version came out a year after the original game. At the same time, in fact, being a demo version. In which one level from the game is available to players.\nProbably, Zoink Games was focusing on the arena - where players can fight.\nIt is also sad that in a year the game has not changed, but remained at the level of the demo version. So we are waiting for the FPS drawdown - where it is not in the full version of the game. AI opponents are also weaker - than in full. This is especially noticeable when the player is above the enemies. At this point, the AI ​​just stands still, while in the original, it constantly runs after you.\nAlso in this version, third-party tasks are cut out that the player performs at the levels. And there is no need for a \"shop\" - since the collected coins for the demo level the player will not be able to spend.\nAs a result: we have a regular demo, which allows you to play fjordball together with your friends.",
